#
# A 2x4 grid of ASICs split into FOUR hosts on a [2,2] host grid: each host owns one row of one
# half, two chips. The machine to ask a one-axis host_topology about -- a declared [2,1] gives two
# ranks of one full row each, and a row here is two hosts wide. Paired with
# test_8asic_2x4_hosts_by_row, which is the same mesh under a [2,1] host grid, where a declared
# [2,2] does fit.
#
#   100 101 | 102 103     h0 h0 | h1 h1
#   --------+--------     ------+------
#   104 105 | 106 107     h2 h2 | h3 h3
#
# Every ASIC gets its own (tray_id, asic_location) = (row+1, col+1) so a PGD can name individual
# chips and pinnings stay injective. Links carry 2 channels and are marked non-local exactly when
# they cross a host boundary. Channels 0/1 run along a row, 2/3 along a column. There are no wrap
# links: these are plain grids.
target_device_type: 0
